    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Cart Expiration Per Product allows you to define how long each product can remain in a customer&#8217;s cart. Once the set time expires, the product is automatically removed.</p>\n<p><strong>Features</strong><br />\n* Set expiry time per product (minutes, hours, or days)<br />\n* Global default expiry<br />\n* Auto-remove expired items<br />\n* Customer notice for removed items<br />\n* Background cleanup with WP-Cron<br />\n* Translation ready</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin folder to <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code>.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the “Plugins” menu.</li>\n<li>Go to <strong>Settings <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Cart Expiration</strong> for defaults.</li>\n<li>Edit any product for per-product expiry.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial Release</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Automatically remove WooCommerce cart items after a custom or global time period.",
    "description": "<p>Cart Expiration Per Product allows you to define how long each product can remain in a customer&#8217;s cart. Once the set time expires, the product is automatically removed.</p>\n<p><strong>Features</strong><br />\n* Set expiry time per product (minutes, hours, or days)<br />\n* Global default expiry<br />\n* Auto-remove expired items<br />\n* Customer notice for removed items<br />\n* Background cleanup with WP-Cron<br />\n* Translation ready</p>\n",
